---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import e from '../data/edition.json';
import receipts from '../data/receipts.json';
import {date} from '../components/format';
const names = Object.fromEntries(e.instruments.map((i:any)=>[i.id,i.name]));
---
<Layout title="Sources & method · Own the Machine"><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">The evidence / {date(e.issue_date)}</div><h1>Show the<br />working.</h1><p>The magazine is assembled from public feeds and dated market history. Selection is deterministic. There is no weekly AI writer and no requirement for an external API key.</p></header><section class="method-grid"><div><h2>Clippings, with limits.</h2><p>The news collector searches public feeds for each instrument and ranks concrete operational developments. Contracts, deliveries, production, financing and launches receive priority. Titles link to the original publisher or its discovery redirect.</p><p>An issuer statement remains an issuer statement. A selected headline has not been independently fact-checked beyond its feed metadata. Filing notices and older material are not treated as this week’s operational stories.</p><p>Primary-source labels identify the publisher, not an independent verification of its claim. Social threads are optional and are not configured.</p></div><div><h2>Returns.</h2><p>1D compares the last two sessions. 1W uses seven calendar days, 1M uses 30, 1Y uses 365 and 5Y uses 1,825. Each target uses the last available session on or before it. YTD starts from the last session on or before 31 December.</p><p>The table reports provider-adjusted close returns in the quote currency. Provider adjustments can include dividends and splits. Stale data, incomplete history and unverified adjustments are flagged or withheld. These are not personal portfolio returns.</p></div><div><h2>Momentum.</h2><p>Portfolio-relative strength uses weighted 3-, 6-, 9- and 12-month performance with weights of 40%, 20%, 20% and 20%. Portfolio Momentum equally averages four percentile ranks inside this collection: portfolio RS, high proximity, annual return and K-ratio.</p><p>Market RS is a separate 1–99 rating calculated by the Momentum Power Scanner across its broad US/UK universe. Stage 2 uses that broad-market rating for gate eight. A stale or unavailable sidecar is shown as unavailable and is never replaced by the portfolio ranking.</p><p>K-ratio measures the slope of a log-price trend relative to its estimated error. Stage 2 is informational, not a trade instruction.</p></div><div><h2>Sunday, and the archive.</h2><p>GitHub Actions is scheduled for Sunday at 22:37 Europe/London, after the broad-market scanner's Sunday run. The platform may start later. A manual run is also available. Successful editions are retained with their receipts and then deployed as static pages.</p><p>There are no account quantities, purchase prices or balances in the public application. To change coverage, edit the holdings file in the repository. Initial identifiers were verified on 21 September 2026.</p></div><div><h2>Photography.</h2><p>{e.image.caption} Credit: {e.image.credit}. This is a technical archive image, not a photograph of a current company event.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={e.image.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Image source ↗</a></p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NASA media usage guidance ↗</a></p></div><div><h2>Quiet is not bad.</h2><p>No selected clipping means no qualifying story was chosen. It does not establish that nothing happened at the company. Feed failures are shown below, separately from successful requests that returned no eligible stories.</p><p>Next-week dates are shown only when collected from an explicit forward event record. This edition has no verified forward calendar. It does not infer event dates from article publication dates.</p></div></section><section class="small-section"><h2>Collection record.</h2><p class="fineprint">{receipts.length} collection receipts. A successful fetch does not guarantee complete coverage of every event.</p><ul class="source-list">{receipts.map((r:any)=><li><span>{names[r.holding_id] || r.holding_id}<br /><small>{r.provider}</small></span><span>{r.url ? <a class="text-link" href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{r.kind} ↗</a> : r.kind}</span><span>{r.status}<br /><small>{r.fetched_at?.slice(0,19).replace('T',' ')} UTC</small></span>{r.error && <code>{r.error}</code>}</li>)}</ul></section></div></Layout>
